<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">James Hargreaves</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1720–<a href="/years/1778">1778</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">James Hargreaves was an English weaver and carpenter from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lancashire">Lancashire</a> who invented the spinning jenny around 1764. The machine let one worker spin several threads at once and greatly increased the output of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cotton">cotton</a> yarn in domestic production. Hand spinners attacked his machines, and he moved to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nottingham">Nottingham</a>, where he patented the jenny in 1770. It was an early invention of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/industrial-revolution">Industrial Revolution</a>.</p></div>
